{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\np='assurance_live_replay_stall_test.go'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='''\t// Commit enough further entries that A's staged commit index is far above its\n\t// snapshot while its own snapshots stay where they are. With MaxAppendEntries\n\t// left at its default of 64 the replay needs 128*64+1 entries to exceed the\n\t// 128-slot channel.\n\tconst extra = 8300'''\nnew='''\t// From here on A's snapshot store fails every attempt. The library logs and\n\t// tolerates that, so A's last snapshot stays where it is while the log grows\n\t// past the bound the replay must cover.\n\tliveStallSnapshotsA.fail = true\n\n\t// Commit enough further entries that A's staged commit index is far above its\n\t// snapshot while its own snapshots stay where they are. With MaxAppendEntries\n\t// left at its default of 64 the replay needs 128*64+1 entries to exceed the\n\t// 128-slot channel.\n\tconst extra = 8300'''\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\nold2='''\t\t\\\"cluster_ids\\\":         \\\"A,B,C\\\",'''\nnew2='''\t\t\\\"snapshot_store_failures\\\": liveStallSnapshotsA.attempts,\n\t\t\\\"snapshot_failures_tolerated\\\": liveStallSnapshotsA.attempts > 0,\n\t\t\\\"cluster_ids\\\":         \\\"A,B,C\\\",'''\nassert old2 in s\ns=s.replace(old2,new2,1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_22-44-04-hashicorp_raft-real-run && cp draft/assurance_live_replay_stall_test.go draft/work/zz_live_test.go && cd draft/work && gofmt -w zz_live_test.go && timeout 300 go test -run TestAssuranceLiveRestoreCommittedLogsStall -count=1 -v . 2>&1 | tail -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
